# ============================================================
# BudgetBot PWA - Environment Variables Reference
# ============================================================
# CRITICAL SECURITY NOTES:
# - NEVER commit actual secrets to git
# - NEVER put bearer tokens or API keys in VITE_* variables
# - VITE_* variables are bundled into the static frontend
# - Auth is now cookie-based — no browser-stored tokens
# ============================================================

# Web App Mode (browser | telegram)
# - browser: Debug mode with fake initData, shows browser back button
# - telegram: Normal operation in Telegram app
VITE_WEB_APP_MODE=browser

# Debug flags (development only — never enable in production)
VITE_DEBUG_API=true
VITE_ENABLE_DEBUG_LOGS=false
VITE_E2E_SILENT_LOGS=false

# ============================================================
# PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT (Cloudflare Pages)
# ============================================================
# DO NOT set VITE_API_BASE_URL in production.
# The app uses same-origin /api/* routing via the Cloudflare Pages middleware.
# The middleware proxies /api/* to BACKEND_URL (set in Cloudflare dashboard).
#
# Required Cloudflare Pages environment variable:
#   BACKEND_URL=https://dev-1.neon-chuckwalla.ts.net
# (Set via: Pages → Settings → Environment variables)

# ============================================================
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# ============================================================
# For local dev, the Vite proxy in vite.config.ts handles /api/* routing.
# The proxy target is https://dev-1.neon-chuckwalla.ts.net.
#
# If you need to override the proxy target, create .env.local (not committed):
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001
#
# The Vite proxy also injects X-Anonymous-Key. To override:
#   SYNC_ANON_API_KEY=<your anon key>

# ============================================================
# FORBIDDEN VARIABLES (DO NOT USE)
# ============================================================
# These MUST NOT be set — they are bundled into static assets:
# - VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (not used, backend handles it)
# - VITE_SYNC_API_KEY (not used, nginx injects it)
# - VITE_SYNC_SERVICE_API_KEY (not used, nginx injects it)
# - Any VITE_* bearer tokens or secrets

# ============================================================
# DEPRECATED VARIABLES (NO LONGER USED)
# ============================================================
# These are kept for reference only — do NOT use them:
# VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME
# VITE_APP_BASE_PATH
# VITE_FIREFLY_TOKEN
# VITE_BASE_URL
# VITE_SYNC_API_KEY
